 "result": "Order of calls, from the server's call to your view (Tessel's own names, in `src/tessel/`):\n\n1. **`Tessel.__call__`** (`app.py:1618`) just delegates to `wsgi_entry`.\n2. **`Tessel.wsgi_entry`** (`app.py:1566`) is the real WSGI app. It runs steps 3–5 below.\n3. **`Tessel.request_context(environ)`** (`app.py:1501`) calls `AppContext.from_environ` (`ctx.py`) to build the context.\n4. **`AppContext.push`** (`ctx.py:416`):\n   - sets the context var and sends the `appcontext_pushed` signal;\n   - opens the session with `_get_session`;\n   - calls `match_request` (`ctx.py:405`) to do URL routing, storing `url_rule`/`view_args` or a `routing_exception`.\n5. **`Tessel.run_full_request`** (`app.py:992`):\n   - sends the `request_started` signal;\n   - calls `preprocess_request` (`app.py:1366`), which runs the before-request functions. If one returns a value, the view is skipped.\n6. **`Tessel.run_view`** (`app.py:966`):\n   - raises any stored routing exception;\n   - auto-replies to OPTIONS;\n   - calls `self.ensure_sync(self.view_functions[rule.endpoint])(**view_args)` (`app.py:990`), which runs your view.\n\nAfter the view, `finalize_request` (`app.py:1021`) builds the response, and `ctx.pop` runs teardown.",
